35,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,The timing data is clear. A full pass takes over an hour. It’s significant.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Mio,,The calendar shows two of us are away most months. That’s a huge gap.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"The chat logs show conflicts start with reminders. It’s about communication, not just dirt.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Rin,,The receipts show we’re buying duplicates. And the kitchen mess is from just two people.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"The grout gets dirty in eleven days. And ""done"" means different things to everyone.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Rin, if only two people cook, maybe they should clean more?","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Ryuji, but if they’re away, who cleans? The absence data is key.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Daisuke, the definition of ""done"" is a major source of friction. We need a standard.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Mio, the cost is low, but the inconsistency is high. We need a fixed plan.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I agree. If we don’t define ""done,"" it will always be a problem.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,The outside firm terms are strict. They need the place tidy before they arrive.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Mio,,The previous tenants’ note says they stopped speaking. We don’t want that.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Mio, exactly. The social cost is too high. We need a system that protects relationships.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Rin,,I think a paid service might be the only way to avoid the arguments.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I am afraid of the cost, but I am more afraid of the arguments.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,Let’s consider the options. We have the data now.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Mio,,I’m leaning towards something that accounts for absences.,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"I want to avoid the ""previous tenants"" scenario.","{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Rin,,I want to stop paying out of pocket.,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,I want predictability.,"{""words"":3,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
